WEBVTT

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.660
Don't shoot! Don't shoot!

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.240
Pulling out a gun isn't fair!

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:19.020
Oh, it was you, Yasaburo-kun!

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.660
You had me there.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:24.000
Mister, you picked that
up somewhere, didn't you?

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.330
How do you know that?

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.540
An acquaintance of mine dropped it.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.200
They've been looking for it.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.210
Please give it back.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.010
Oh, is that so?

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:36.260
But now, it's one of my favorite belongings.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.190
I'm not going to give it back
just because you ask nicely.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.400
Pulling out a gun isn't fair.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.840
I don't play fair.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.520
I'm a cheater.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:55.210
To be a true cheater,

00:00:55.210 --> 00:01:00.220
you have to have every
unfair trick up your sleeve.

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:10.290
That should be enough.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.120
Until I can get an answer that I like,

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:18.340
I'm going to hold onto your moon.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.030
Also, that was a splendid oni.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:23.420
I was blown away.

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.940
I thought that an oni from Hell
might scare you a bit.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.400
Did you happen to see that painting of Hell?

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:30.650
I did.

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:31.800
Damn it.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.780
I knew it was still in that house.

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:37.400
Tenmaya-san, you were in Hell, right?

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:40.750
Jyurojin's illusions got the better of me.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.030
Why did you make Jyurojin angry?

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:47.820
I apparently know nothing about you.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:49.790
How do you know Jyurojin?

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:52.460
Someone named Benten introduced me to him.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:54.050
Benten?!

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.340
That woman is the cause of all this!

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:00.550
She started putting lies
and half-truths into Jyurojin's head!

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.860
True, she's beautiful.

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:05.720
True, she's charming.

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:08.850
True, she's completely out of my league!

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:13.360
But that doesn't mean she'll get
away with sending me to Hell!

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.820
I am the great Tenmaya!

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:18.950
I'm not burying my bones in Hell
when I've got a score to settle!

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:20.700
Curse that woman.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:23.470
The next time I see her, she'll be sorr—

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.460
It's been a while.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:10.980
<b>Episode Three
The Scent of Europe</b>

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:14.270
It's been a while, Tenmaya-san.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:19.280
<b>The Beautiful Live Longer</b>

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:18.460
I'm glad to find you well.

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:20.880
Benten-sama...

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:23.530
You should become a lecturer.

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:27.190
Well, well, if it isn't Benten-sama.

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:29.540
How much of our conversation
did you happen to hear?

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:33.160
Right around when you said
that I was out of your league.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:36.420
I've heard your most valued opinion.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:39.340
Please forget everything I said afterward.

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:42.800
He said that you'd be sorry
the next time he saw you.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:45.280
What are you talking about, Yasaburo-kun?!

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:47.760
That was just a thing people always say!

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:51.560
You know how you say stuff like that
to someone you're interested in?

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:53.980
Oh, my!

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:57.880
Your skull could shatter
at any moment, Tenmaya-san.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:59.980
Would you like to go to Hell again?

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:01.340
I wouldn't dream of it!

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:07.360
Not when I'm experiencing Heaven
right under your foot, Benten-sama.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:11.370
To think that I'd see your face
the moment I came home.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:14.780
Let's let the Styx wash our past
under the bridge and into Hell,

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:17.890
and let's just get along.

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:19.890
What ever shall I do?

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:23.830
After all, I hate you like poison.

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:24.700
Oh?

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:25.420
Oh, my.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:27.330
That's rather lovely.

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:31.780
Such a beautiful moon...

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:33.090
Isn't it, Yasaburo?

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:35.120
It is, of course.

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:37.100
It's my moon.

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:38.810
Oh, is it?

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:41.340
I'd love to put it up in my house.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:44.240
I've always wanted one of my own.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:46.510
Please don't.

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:50.200
A tanuki without a moon at night
wouldn't have a belly to drum on.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:53.680
You've never drummed
your belly for me before.

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:23.990
Tenmaya-san's going to die.

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:27.540
He wouldn't die from something like that.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.660
It truly is a beautiful moon.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.010
Take my luggage for me, Yasaburo.

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:41.790
I'm going to go say hello to our master.

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:43.590
That's a great idea.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.860
I'm sure he'll be very happy.

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:51.800
Benten-sama, may I ask something?

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:53.980
What is it, Yasaburo?

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:58.390
Would you mind returning my moon to me?

00:06:58.690 --> 00:06:59.590
Oh, dear.

00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:01.940
Do I really have to give it back?

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:04.810
I humbly ask that you do.

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:08.650
It would be very hard living through
dark nights without the moon's light.

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:10.650
Should I, now?

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:13.780
I mean, I finally got my hands on the moon.

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:23.170
Thank you very much, Benten-sama.

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:26.840
Don't you have something else to say?

00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:29.300
You're such a thoughtless tanuki.

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:31.060
What would that be?

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:34.750
Say that you missed me, Yasaburo.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:38.400
I missed you very much.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:41.830
Welcome back, Benten-sama.

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:44.480
I've come home.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:48.020
Aren't things getting interesting, Yasaburo?

00:07:57.450 --> 00:08:00.640
See where this step is a little chipped?

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:02.920
I did this by jumping off it.

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:04.580
You're lying.

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:07.730
I'm not lying at all.

00:08:07.730 --> 00:08:11.640
I ran these steps thousands of times.
They were bound to chip.

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:13.590
I was running up these stairs

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:16.640
when So-san first climbed up here.

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:19.250
He said he was from the
Bamboo Shoot Expedition Squad.

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:22.120
It's not "bamboo shoot," it's "tsuchinoko."

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:23.600
Right, right. "Tsuchinoko."

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:30.980
<b>Tanukidanisan Fudo-in Temple</b>

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:28.050
So Father went out to catch a tsuchinoko,

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:30.020
but caught your heart instead.

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:42.000
Hello.

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:48.500
Well, well, if it isn't Tousen.

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:52.010
It's been a long time since
I've seen you as well, Yasaburo.

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:54.410
It's been a while, Nii-san.

00:08:54.830 --> 00:08:57.680
I came here to ask a favor from Mother.

00:08:57.680 --> 00:08:59.290
I see. I see.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:02.140
Then let's go forth.

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:14.990
Namu, namu...

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:18.740
Namu, namu...

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:21.490
Namu, namu...

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:30.170
Mother, it is I, Tousen.

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:33.420
Oh, my.

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:35.700
Is that you, Tousen?

00:09:36.230 --> 00:09:39.060
It is your daughter, Tousen.

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:41.440
I apologize if I have awakened you.

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:45.040
There's no need to apologize.

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:48.690
I wasn't asleep.

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:49.680
That's good.

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:51.940
So you weren't asleep, Mother.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:53.780
Yes.

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:57.290
I was just thinking about fun things.

00:09:57.290 --> 00:09:58.880
Fun things?

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:01.870
Like clear water,

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:06.080
or when you can see green leaves
reflected upon that water,

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:10.540
or when you can see through those
leaves because of the sunlight.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:13.710
You were thinking about
such wonderful things, Mother.

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:17.770
Yes, I am your mother.

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:20.160
Oh, dear.

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:22.820
I thought you went off to be married.

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:24.780
I did indeed go off to be married.

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:27.670
I knew it was true.

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:30.730
So you're living happily?

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:33.110
I am living happily.

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:34.880
Sniff, sniff.

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:37.750
You have a lovely scent about you.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:41.820
Say, would you smell me?

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:46.400
Do I smell strange?

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:48.690
Of course not.

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:50.460
You smell very lovely.

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:51.830
I knew it.

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:54.960
I knew I wouldn't smell strange.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:58.670
But I worry about it from time to time.

00:10:59.150 --> 00:11:00.720
You see, Mother,

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:03.040
I have a question I'd like to ask you.

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:04.180
What's that?

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:07.150
There's a tanuki that spent
too much time as a frog

00:11:07.150 --> 00:11:10.260
and can't transform back anymore.

00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:13.460
Is there a way to let him
be able to transform again?

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:15.350
Hmm...

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:17.520
If he's unable to transform,

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:21.470
it means that the water
at the bottom of his belly is dry.

00:11:21.470 --> 00:11:24.200
But he lives at the bottom of a well.

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:27.080
There's plenty of water there.

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:31.470
Well water and the water
at the bottom of your belly

00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:32.900
are a little different.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:34.940
What should we do?

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:37.810
I'll let you know about a great medicine.

00:11:38.270 --> 00:11:41.440
You drink it while you practice transforming.

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:43.590
Toichiro.

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:48.560
Please wait a while.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:50.920
I'll prepare the medicine immediately.

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:52.550
Thank you.

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:55.690
Who's that over there?

00:11:56.930 --> 00:11:58.750
I'm just a passing tanuki.

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:00.450
My name is Yasaburo.

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:03.190
Oh, hello, dear.

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:05.510
Is this the first time we've met?

00:12:05.510 --> 00:12:08.210
I think we've met a number of times before.

00:12:08.210 --> 00:12:09.130
I knew it.

00:12:09.130 --> 00:12:10.700
That's what I thought.

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:14.010
Could you come a little closer?

00:12:16.490 --> 00:12:17.850
Sniff, sniff.

00:12:18.290 --> 00:12:22.630
My eyes can't see anymore.

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:25.520
It happened without warning.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:29.940
But I can see water flowing.

00:12:29.940 --> 00:12:34.780
This world is a giant river,
and we all flow with it together.

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:39.270
It appears that the flow of the river
isn't very good right now.

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:42.190
Is it something like being constipated?

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:44.740
Yes, it's something like that.

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:47.520
Well, that's not very pleasant.

00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:50.620
Don't speak of it as though
it doesn't concern you.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:54.500
You'll have to work hard to overcome it.

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:59.390
Keep your eyes open and your fur groomed.

00:12:59.390 --> 00:13:02.740
And make sure you cause some trouble.

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:04.810
Make sure you cause a lot of it.

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:09.540
That's all I wanted to say.

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:11.030
The end.

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:25.400
You'll have to work hard to overcome it.

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:30.970
Your grandmother said some mysterious things.

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:33.160
I wonder what I'm supposed to work harder at.

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:34.790
I haven't a clue.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:38.540
It really is hot out today.

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:40.910
Well, it is summer.

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:44.550
Speaking of summer, the Gozan
Farewell Bonfire is coming up.

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:47.030
I hope this year's will be fun, too.

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:50.450
Speaking of which, is Yaichiro
getting the luxury liner?

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:51.850
Yes.

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:54.180
He said he was going to rent an envoy ship.

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:56.140
He's been visiting Nara nonstop.

00:13:57.210 --> 00:13:59.670
Yaichiro is so busy.

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:02.230
The shogi tournament, the luxury liner...

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:04.610
You should help your brother out.

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:06.240
No way.

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:07.260
Jeez...

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:14.080
Nii-sa— Whoa!

00:14:14.610 --> 00:14:16.650
Oh, Yasaburo.

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:21.080
What are you doing, Nii-san?

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:22.780
Well...

00:14:22.780 --> 00:14:25.460
I was just practicing my transformations.

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:27.720
Do you think you've got it back?

00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:29.500
Hard to say.

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:32.460
I can transform into the Eizan train,

00:14:32.460 --> 00:14:35.040
but I'm having no luck with anything else.

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:40.650
What's this?

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:44.010
I'm going to enter the shogi tournament,

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:46.700
so I've been practicing some tsumeshogi.

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:50.080
So, what brings you here today?

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:51.530
Oh, right.

00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:54.470
What's this?

00:14:54.470 --> 00:14:57.170
I brought some medicine from Grandmother.

00:14:57.590 --> 00:15:00.540
It wouldn't hurt for you to
be able to transform again sooner.

00:15:01.220 --> 00:15:03.360
Grandmother, eh?

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:04.410
Right.

00:15:04.410 --> 00:15:06.540
I'll gladly use it.

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:09.930
When I'm able to transform again,
I should go thank her.

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:13.620
They do say that medicine
from Tanukidani Fudo works well.

00:15:13.620 --> 00:15:17.210
By the way, Yasaburo,
have you heard about the Nidaime?

00:15:17.210 --> 00:15:18.130
What about him?

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:20.970
Apparently, he checked out of the hotel.

00:15:20.970 --> 00:15:21.710
Huh?

00:15:22.660 --> 00:15:25.330
This is the first I've heard about that.

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:28.990
<b>Tanukidanisan Fudo-in Temple</b>

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:34.330
Is he really here?

00:15:34.880 --> 00:15:37.880
Apparently, he moved from
the hotel to this rooftop.

00:15:43.310 --> 00:15:45.220
Hold on a sec, Yashiro.

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:21.180
Hello there.

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:23.790
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:26.710
I'm surprised you're ironing in this heat.

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:28.730
Aren't you hot?

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:30.480
It is indeed hot.

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:33.550
By the way, who's this with you?

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:38.400
I humbly appear before you as
Shimogamo Soichiro's fourth son,

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:40.560
Shimogamo Yashiro.

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:44.720
To celebrate your moving here,
I present you with this gift.

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:48.080
Well, thank you.

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:51.590
Now, then.

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:55.040
Do you furballs have some time?

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:57.670
We have more time than
we know what to do with.

00:16:57.670 --> 00:16:58.900
Very good.

00:16:58.900 --> 00:17:00.790
As thanks for the moving gift,

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:04.090
I will invite you furballs to afternoon tea.

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:26.080
Hot!

00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:32.310
Is it not to your liking?

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:34.540
That's not the case.

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:35.580
It's delicious.

00:17:36.310 --> 00:17:39.660
It's just that I prefer not
to dirty my hands while I eat.

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:44.120
This is a rather high-class place.

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:48.250
Apparently, it's a villa that
belonged to some tanuki elite.

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:51.240
When I first found it,
it reeked strongly of tanuki,

00:17:51.240 --> 00:17:54.260
but I've had it remodeled,
so I don't mind it anymore.

00:17:54.690 --> 00:17:58.510
Could it have been Kinkaku and Ginkaku
who provided you with this place?

00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:00.810
That's exactly right.

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:03.830
Apparently, after their father left Kyoto,

00:18:03.830 --> 00:18:06.020
no one else was using it.

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:09.440
You've incurred a debt
to a rather troublesome pair.

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:11.920
Oh, there is no debt.

00:18:11.920 --> 00:18:15.110
They took a bowl filled with gold.

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:17.080
They are faithful to their greed.

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:18.710
Our account is settled.

00:18:18.710 --> 00:18:21.660
Personally, I find you far more troublesome.

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:26.040
You're wasting your tengu abilities.

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:29.520
It wouldn't hurt
to let loose once in a while.

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:33.350
You say some truly unsettling things.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:36.050
However, I am not a tengu.

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:38.810
There you go, being stubborn again.

00:18:39.210 --> 00:18:41.550
I am quite busy, you know?

00:18:42.030 --> 00:18:44.060
I'm not even done cleaning this room yet.

00:18:44.380 --> 00:18:45.860
What do you mean?

00:18:45.860 --> 00:18:50.020
This is night and day compared to
the chaos that is Akadama-sensei's apartment.

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:57.530
You should just burn that place down.

00:18:57.860 --> 00:18:59.250
It'll be much cleaner.

00:19:01.360 --> 00:19:02.870
<b>Advanced</b>

00:19:01.360 --> 00:19:02.870
<b>Electromagnetism</b>

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:05.230
Hey, Yashiro, you're being rude.

00:19:05.230 --> 00:19:07.040
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:08.350
I don't mind.

00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:10.230
Electromagnetism, eh?

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:11.010
Yes.

00:19:11.010 --> 00:19:14.420
I also researched it obsessively at one time.

00:19:14.690 --> 00:19:15.560
I know.

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:19.260
I'll give Yashiro-kun something
to protect his eyes.

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:23.930
Here you go.

00:19:27.860 --> 00:19:29.140
Go on and take them.

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:31.300
Thank you.

00:19:41.710 --> 00:19:43.430
My friendly furballs,

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:45.580
could I ask you to take your leave soon?

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:48.490
We apologize for staying so long.

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:51.040
Before I take my walk,

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:53.420
I'd like to take a nap on my chaise.

00:20:13.170 --> 00:20:15.430
That would be Benten-sama.

00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:17.560
Oh, I see.

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:22.990
May I help you?

00:20:23.510 --> 00:20:24.650
Miss,

00:20:24.650 --> 00:20:27.320
My apologies for disturbing
your comfortable rest,

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:29.990
but I'd like my chaise back.

00:20:30.570 --> 00:20:35.020
I must take my afternoon nap soon.

00:20:35.650 --> 00:20:39.000
Oh, but I'm using it.

00:20:39.350 --> 00:20:43.570
That is my beloved chaise, Miss.

00:20:43.570 --> 00:20:44.870
I'm sure it is.

00:20:45.290 --> 00:20:47.990
It is amazingly comfortable.

00:20:48.630 --> 00:20:50.520
I could fall asleep at any moment.

00:21:03.430 --> 00:21:05.800
Very well, Miss.

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:08.570
Stay as you are. Stay as you are.

00:21:16.030 --> 00:21:19.120
I do apologize for your discomfort, Miss.

00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:23.300
But no matter how comfortable you may feel,

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:26.130
the problem at hand right now

00:21:27.070 --> 00:21:30.850
is that I do not feel comfortable.

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:37.000
Well, then. Farewell.

00:21:37.590 --> 00:21:38.880
Good night.

00:21:40.490 --> 00:21:43.520
<i>Long ago, a wise, old tanuki once said...</i>

00:21:44.390 --> 00:21:46.570
<i>"Tengu getting involved in tanuki disputes...</i>

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:48.340
<i>this is no good."</i>

00:21:48.980 --> 00:21:50.990
<i>"Tanuki getting involved in tengu disputes...</i>

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:53.000
<i>this is no good, either."</i>

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:58.960
I didn't like that saying.

00:23:30.910 --> 00:23:33.010
People who play shogi are wonderful.

00:23:33.470 --> 00:23:34.010
What?

00:23:34.010 --> 00:23:35.100
You don't know the game?

00:23:35.490 --> 00:23:36.880
Then let's play!

00:23:36.880 --> 00:23:38.110
It's fun!

00:23:37.640 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Episode Four
The Tanuki Shogi Tournament</b>

00:23:38.110 --> 00:23:39.940
It'll definitely be fun!
